          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Getting tilted",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ],
              "colour": "#268cff"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " Bob plays two tennis games against another player. They both start with an equal chance of winning. If Bob wins the first game, he gets confident and has a 75% chance of winning the second game. If Bob loses the first game, he loses his confidence and has a 10% chance of winning the second game. What is the probability that Bob",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q18-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p33-q18-a-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "wins the second game, given he loses the first game.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{10}$",
          "worked": "The first-game loss selects the branch with a 10% chance of winning the second game.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{second win}\\mid\\text{first loss})&=0.10\\\\P(\\text{second win}\\mid\\text{first loss})&=\\frac{1}{10}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q18-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p33-q18-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "loses the second game, given he wins the first game.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{4}$",
          "worked": "Use the complement of winning on the first-win branch.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{second loss}\\mid\\text{first win})&=1-0.75\\\\P(\\text{second loss}\\mid\\text{first win})&=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q18-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
